# CORRECTED 2026-09-05 (see the file-header banner above): the 2026-09-04
# advice that used to live here -- "quote the value if it has a space,
# systemd/bash both preserve it verbatim" -- was WRONG and caused a real
# ~1-hour NWWS-OI outage (silent SASL not-authorized on every reconnect,
# masked by a separate heartbeat bug -- see ingest/nwws.py). The value is
# NOT read via systemd's EnvironmentFile= parser at all; Podman Quadlet
# turns that directive into `podman run --env-file`, and podman's
# --env-file format does not strip quotes -- confirmed live via
# `podman exec ... env`, the literal quote characters were part of the
# password. NEVER quote this value, even if it contains a space -- podman
# preserves internal spaces perfectly fine unquoted (no shell involved,
# no word-splitting). If a value with a space ever needs a space at all,
# just write it bare.
NWWS_JID=CHANGE_ME
NWWS_PASSWORD=CHANGE_ME


